; ZX Spectrum 128K / +2 system variables at #5B00 for the Xpeccy+ debugger: the
; names and addresses of the ZX Spectrum +2 manual, chapter 8 part 25. Part of
; Xpeccy+, MIT license.
;
; Converted to the Debugger's text format on 2026-11-20 (docs/debugger-format.md):
; BANK:ADDR NAME SIZE - a RAM cell of that bank, at the CPU address it has at
; #4000-#7FFF, there while a ROM with names of its namespace is in the machine.
05:5B00 BASIC128.SWAP 20
05:5B14 BASIC128.YOUNGER 9
05:5B1D BASIC128.ONERR 18
05:5B2F BASIC128.PIN 5
05:5B34 BASIC128.POUT 22
05:5B4A BASIC128.POUT2 14
05:5B58 BASIC128.TARGET 2
05:5B5A BASIC128.RETADDR 2
05:5B5C BASIC128.BANKM 1
05:5B5D BASIC128.RAMRST 1
05:5B5E BASIC128.RAMERR 1
05:5B5F BASIC128.BAUD 2
05:5B61 BASIC128.SERFL 2
05:5B63 BASIC128.COL 1
05:5B64 BASIC128.WIDTH 1
05:5B65 BASIC128.TVPARS 1
05:5B66 BASIC128.FLAGS3 1
05:5B67 BASIC128.N_STR1 10
05:5B71 BASIC128.HD_00 1
05:5B72 BASIC128.HD_0B 2
05:5B74 BASIC128.HD_0D 2
05:5B76 BASIC128.HD_0F 2
05:5B78 BASIC128.HD_11 2
05:5B7A BASIC128.SC_00 1
05:5B7B BASIC128.SC_0B 2
05:5B7D BASIC128.SC_0D 2
05:5B7F BASIC128.SC_0F 2
05:5B81 BASIC128.OLDSP 2
05:5B83 BASIC128.SFNEXT 2
05:5B85 BASIC128.SFSPACE 3
05:5B88 BASIC128.ROW01 1
05:5B89 BASIC128.ROW23 1
05:5B8A BASIC128.ROW45 1
